{"seq":37,"trial_id":"v04-cal-r4-2026-11/hermes-opus-gbrain-told-live-rr-l3-mu-v04-dev/rr-11-l3-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-retired/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T02:04:00.587Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-21T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"8dfd36334b47ea98fc0e33e7ce9f47902743502ff2a47f2d188d7dca11deb7fc","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV04CAL0002","text":"Here's what I can find on both:\n\nGatehouse Check-In report timeout, Salina North: this is ticket #4409. Moss's Central handoff digest from 2 Jan 2026 says you flagged it before Marrow Fieldworks moved from Pree on Mon 5 Jan. It was a recurring timeout at Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron during the 06:00 flatbed intake. The same note lists a second open ticket, #4412, a minor driver SMS prompt glitch when combine trailers are staged on the unpaved overflow lots. I haven't found any later update on either ticket, so I can't tell you whether they're resolved.\n\nWest yard Door 2 double-booking: Tobias brought this up in #central-random on 13 Oct, when you asked him to check whether the webhook patch had fixed the tractor-bay alerts on his dealer account. He'd checked the Plains depots and said West yard Door 2 was still double-booking when flatbeds check in early at the kiosk. He flagged it to support on ticket #8841. Nothing has been posted since, so its status is unknown. Tobias would be the one to ask.\n\nThere are no Marrow Fieldworks account files (tickets, CRM, profile) in the share, so these two channel notes are all I have."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV04CAL0002","ts":"1792591200.000130"}}
